#! ia 1.0

@capability task-method
  meaning
    says "Work with task records under the IA methodology: the task-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a task. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a task?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook task-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook task-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with task records, each one owner's action toward exactly one milestone, whose readiness ia next computes and the record never stores: orient through ia position --word task and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with task records?"
  subject
    subject-word task
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word task at the seat the work concerns, read the task records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary task --schema for the sections and fields a task carries."
      Inference means "Find the milestone the task serves and the plan above it, and run ia next --seat <plan> to see which tasks are ready, blocked or waiting, and on what."
      Decision means "task is a word of work-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/work-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these task records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the task must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Give the task one owner and exactly one milestone, and name what it requires (decisions, other tasks) and what it cites, so ia next can order it; a task that rests on an open decision requires that decision."
      Decision means "Extend an existing task through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the task will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the task; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the task's owner, milestone and requirements, never a stored ready or done status; the work it does lands in the records and files it changes."
      Decision means "Change task records only through ia preview task <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Run ia next again and confirm the task's verdict and basis are what the plan expected; when the task closes its milestone, reconcile the milestone."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the task, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability plan-method
  meaning
    says "Work with plan records under the IA methodology: the plan-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a plan. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a plan?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook plan-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook plan-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with plan records, each an arrangement of milestones toward an intent, which heads the work hierarchy, has no parent and does not nest: orient through ia position --word plan and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with plan records?"
  subject
    subject-word plan
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word plan at the seat the work concerns, read the plan records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary plan --schema for the sections and fields a plan carries."
      Inference means "Read the plan's intent and milestones, and run ia next --seat <plan> for the delivery order of its tasks."
      Decision means "plan is a word of work-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/work-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these plan records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the plan must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Arrange the outcome as milestones with exit criteria under one plan; when the work needs a second arrangement, author a second plan rather than nesting one."
      Decision means "Extend an existing plan through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the plan will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the plan; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the plan with its intent before its milestones, and change an existing plan field by field with --set rather than rewriting it."
      Decision means "Change plan records only through ia preview plan <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that every milestone belongs to this plan and every task to one milestone, and that ia next orders them as intended."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the plan, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability milestone-method
  meaning
    says "Work with milestone records under the IA methodology: the milestone-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a milestone. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a milestone?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook milestone-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook milestone-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with milestone records, each an outcome with an exit criterion inside exactly one plan, naming a condition rather than the work toward it: orient through ia position --word milestone and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with milestone records?"
  subject
    subject-word milestone
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word milestone at the seat the work concerns, read the milestone records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary milestone --schema for the sections and fields a milestone carries."
      Inference means "Read the milestone's plan, its exit criterion and the tasks that point at it."
      Decision means "milestone is a word of work-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/work-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these milestone records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the milestone must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "State the exit criterion as a condition someone can observe, not as the work toward it, and place the milestone in exactly one plan."
      Decision means "Extend an existing milestone through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the milestone will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the milestone; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the milestone with its plan and exit criterion, and leave the work toward it to tasks."
      Decision means "Change milestone records only through ia preview milestone <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Judge the milestone met only against its exit criterion and the evidence that shows it, and reconcile the tasks that remain open under it."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the milestone, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability decision-method
  meaning
    says "Work with decision records under the IA methodology: the decision-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a decision. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a decision?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook decision-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook decision-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with decision records, each a choice that is needed or has been made: the question, options and decider, and once made, the choice and rationale: orient through ia position --word decision and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with decision records?"
  subject
    subject-word decision
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word decision at the seat the work concerns, read the decision records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary decision --schema for the sections and fields a decision carries."
      Inference means "Read the decision's question, options and decider, and whether it has a choice; a decision with no choice is open, and work that requires it waits."
      Decision means "decision is a word of work-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/work-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these decision records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the decision must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Frame the question, the options with their consequences and the decider; bring it to the decider with a recommendation, and keep the independent work moving."
      Decision means "Extend an existing decision through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the decision will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the decision; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author an open decision with its question, options and decider; record the choice and rationale only once the decider has made it, never on their behalf."
      Decision means "Change decision records only through ia preview decision <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Reconcile what the choice changes (the tasks that required it, the specs it grounds, any layer that rested on it), as method-reconcile-on-change describes."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the decision, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability spec-method
  meaning
    says "Work with spec records under the IA methodology: the spec-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a spec. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a spec?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook spec-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook spec-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with spec records, each a maintained specification with an explicit status and at most one same-word successor: orient through ia position --word spec and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with spec records?"
  subject
    subject-word spec
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word spec at the seat the work concerns, read the spec records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary spec --schema for the sections and fields a spec carries."
      Inference means "Read the spec's status, the decisions that ground it and any successor; a spec that is not accepted is a provisional foundation, and the ceiling law applies."
      Decision means "spec is a word of work-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/work-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these spec records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the spec must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide whether the change revises the spec, supersedes it with one successor or needs a decision first; work that rests on a draft goes one layer deep."
      Decision means "Extend an existing spec through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the spec will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the spec; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the spec with its status and source locator, and supersede an accepted spec through its one successor rather than rewriting it in place."
      Decision means "Change spec records only through ia preview spec <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Re-read the work that cites the spec, and reconcile it with the status and content that were ratified."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the spec, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
